@startuml seq_dia_security_reset
title SC-DIA-03 - Security access level 0x01 and ECU reset (application)

participant "UDS tester" as Tester
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over Tester, TCU
Covers: SYS-DIA-002, SYS-STA-001, SYS-ACT-004, SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-007, SIM-PLT-004
UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9 (can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over TCU: control active, default session
Tester -> TCU : 27 01
TCU --> Tester : 7F 27 7F
note right: 27 only in the extended session (reprogramming section 3)
Tester -> TCU : 10 03
TCU --> Tester : 50 03 00 32 01 F4

== security access level 0x01 ==
Tester -> TCU : 27 01
TCU --> Tester : 67 01 <seed, 4 bytes>
note right: seed = free-running 32-bit timer, 0 replaced by 1\n(reprogramming section 3)
Tester -> Tester : key = rotl32(seed, 7) XOR 0x5A3C_C3A5
alt correct key
  Tester -> TCU : 27 02 <key, 4 bytes>
  TCU --> Tester : 67 02
  note right: level 0x01 unlocked; it unlocks nothing in v1\n(reserved for later writes with 2E)
  opt seed requested again while unlocked
    Tester -> TCU : 27 01
    TCU --> Tester : 67 01 00 00 00 00
    note right: seed 0 = already unlocked
  end
else wrong key, 3 attempts
  Tester -> TCU : 27 02 <wrong key>
  TCU --> Tester : 7F 27 35
  note right: invalidKey (ISO 14229-1), attempts 1 and 2
  Tester -> TCU : 27 01 / 27 02 <wrong key> (third attempt)
  TCU --> Tester : 7F 27 36
  Tester -> TCU : 27 01 (within 10 s)
  TCU --> Tester : 7F 27 37
  note right: same lockout rule as level 0x11:\n36 on the third failure, 37 for 10 s\n(reprogramming section 3, SYS-BOOT-005)
end

== ECU reset ==
Tester -> TCU : 11 01
TCU --> Tester : 51 01
TCU -> TCU : software reset (power cycle): session, security state, limp-home,\nfault bits and volatile DTC memory cleared (SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-007)
... 50 ms without TCU_Actuators ...
Plant -> Plant : hydraulic default (SIM-PLT-004)
TCU -> TCU : PBL check, 50 ms boot window, application Init (SC-STA-01)
TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators every 10 ms, TCU_Status every 100 ms
note right of TCU: control active <= 500 ms after the reset (SYS-STA-001);\nnothing transmitted before (SYS-ACT-004)
@enduml
